@*
    REQ-UI-072 / REQ-FN-139 — the Price providers screen (docs/mockups/prices.html).

    Where a rate comes from, and how current it is. The framework records what it MEASURED — tokens,
    per model, per run — and never writes a price into a record; turning tokens into money is a
    reporting job, which is why the price list lives here. A rate changing re-prices every run ever
    recorded, and no record was ever wrong.

    Two claims are kept apart on this page and never merged. A rate read from a provider's own endpoint
    is data; a rate typed from a provider's published page is a person's reading of it. Both are
    legitimate, so every provider carries a label saying which it is (`prices-kind-{id}`, a blue badge
    for an endpoint and a grey one for a typed page) and the date it was last checked, rather than
    appearing as bare authority. Only OpenRouter publishes rates as an endpoint today.

    Rebuilt 2026-09-11 against the mockup drawn after the first build: the type label, the pager
    (`prices-page-prev-{id}` / `prices-page-next-{id}`, five rates a page) and the model filter on a long
    provider (`prices-filter-{id}`) were missing, and at 390px the rate headers ran together and model ids
    broke mid-name. Each provider's table is now a DataTable fed one page at a time by PriceRatePage.

    Taken up on TrBlazeUI 2.1.0-ci.10 (2026-09-12): the figure columns align through the column's own
    `Align`, the endpoint claim is a real `BadgeVariant.Info`, the layout rows are the shipped
    responsive utilities, and the select paints its own chevron again. The scoped sheet is what is
    left over once those are gone.
*@
@page "/prices"
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text.Json
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using TfLens.Core.Metrics
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.InputGroup
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.NativeSelect
@inject IOptions<TfLensOptions> objOptions
@inject IHttpClientFactory objHttpClientFactory

<PageTitle>Price providers · TfLens</PageTitle>

<div class="tflens-stack tflens-prices">

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <div>
            <TypographyH2>Price providers</TypographyH2>
            <TypographyMuted>
                Published list rates, used to price measured tokens. A price, never a bill.
            </TypographyMuted>
        </div>
        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="prices-model-count">@CountLabel</Badge>
    </div>

    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Info" data-testid="prices-standing-note">
        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
        <AlertTitle>Nobody was billed these amounts</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
            These are <strong>published rates</strong> applied to tokens that were measured. They are
            reported as a <strong>list price</strong> and never as spend. The only measured dollars in
            TfLens come from a provider that billed per token; a flat monthly plan bills nothing extra,
            so its marginal cost is a true zero and never appears here. Applying a change rewrites
            <code>@objOptions.Value.PricesPath</code>, which every figure is priced from.
        </AlertDescription>
    </Alert>

    @if (objClashes.Count > 0)
    {
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" data-testid="prices-clashes">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>@objClashes.Count model id(s) priced by more than one provider</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                @string.Join(", ", objClashes). The first provider listed wins and the rest are ignored —
                never averaged, because the mean of two published rates is a number nobody publishes.
                Remove the duplicate from whichever provider should not own it.
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    }

    @if (objIsLoading)
    {
        for (var vSkeleton = 0; vSkeleton < 3; vSkeleton++)
        {
            <Card>
                <CardHeader>
                    <Skeleton Class="h-5 w-40" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-64" />
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent>
                    <Skeleton Class="h-16 w-full" />
                </CardContent>
            </Card>
        }
    }

    @foreach (var vProvider in objProviders)
    {
        var vPage = PageFor(vProvider);

        <Card data-testid="@($"prices-provider-{vProvider.Id}")">
            <CardHeader Class="tflens-prices-cardhead">
                <div class="flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col items-start gap-3 md:flex-row md:justify-between">
                    <div class="min-w-0">
                        <CardTitle Class="text-base">@vProvider.Name</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            @if (vProvider.SourceUrl is { Length: > 0 } vSource)
                            {
                                <a class="tflens-prices-source" href="@vSource" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@vSource</a>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>no published page recorded</span>
                            }
                        </CardDescription>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-start gap-2 md:justify-end">
                        @* The two claims are two different badges, never one badge with two words: a
                           blue "read from its endpoint" and a grey "typed from the published page".
                           The blue is the library's own Info variant, which is the tone the mockup
                           draws it in. *@
                        @if (IsEndpoint(vProvider))
                        {
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Info"
                                   data-testid="@($"prices-kind-{vProvider.Id}")">read from its endpoint</Badge>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary"
                                   data-testid="@($"prices-kind-{vProvider.Id}")">typed from the published page</Badge>
                        }
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="@($"prices-checked-{vProvider.Id}")">
                            @CheckedLabel(vProvider)
                        </Badge>
                        @if (IsEndpoint(vProvider) && vProvider.ApiUrl is { Length: > 0 })
                        {
                            <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline"
                                    Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                    Disabled="@objIsBusy"
                                    data-testid="@($"prices-refresh-{vProvider.Id}")"
                                    OnClick="() => RefreshAsync(vProvider)">
                                <LucideIcon Name="refresh-cw" Size="16" />
                                Refresh
                            </Button>
                        }
                        <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                Disabled="@objIsBusy"
                                data-testid="@($"prices-remove-{vProvider.Id}")"
                                OnClick="() => RemoveAsync(vProvider)">
                            Remove
                        </Button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>

            @if (vProvider.Models.Count == 0)
            {
                <CardContent>
                    <TypographyMuted>
                        No rates yet. @(IsEndpoint(vProvider)
                            ? "Refresh to read them from the endpoint."
                            : "Add a model below.") A model with no rate is left out of every money
                        figure and counted as unpriced — never priced at zero.
                    </TypographyMuted>
                </CardContent>
            }
            else
            {
                if (PriceRatePage.NeedsFilter(vProvider.Models.Count))
                {
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0 tflens-prices-cardbody">
                        <div class="tflens-prices-filter">
                            <InputGroup>
                                <InputGroupAddon Align="InputGroupAlign.InlineStart">
                                    <LucideIcon Name="search" Size="16" />
                                </InputGroupAddon>
                                <InputGroupInput Value="@FilterOf(vProvider)"
                                                 ValueChanged="@((string? aText) => OnFilterChanged(vProvider, aText))"
                                                 Placeholder="Filter models…"
                                                 AriaLabel="@($"Filter {vProvider.Name} models")"
                                                 data-testid="@($"prices-filter-{vProvider.Id}")" />
                            </InputGroup>
                        </div>
                    </CardContent>
                }

                <CardContent Class="tflens-prices-flush">
                    @if (vPage.Rows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <TypographyMuted Class="tflens-prices-nomatch">
                            No model id contains “@FilterOf(vProvider)”.
                        </TypographyMuted>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @* The table is handed exactly one page of rates, so pagination is off and every
                           row it is given is drawn. Compact density sets the cell padding and each
                           column's own classes are merged over it, so the header and body cells carry
                           the mockup's 10/16 and 12/16 without any page CSS reaching into the grid. *@
                        <DataTable TData="PriceProviderModel"
                                   Data="@vPage.Rows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   Density="DataTableDensity.Compact"
                                   AriaLabel="@($"{vProvider.Name} rates")"
                                   data-testid="@($"prices-table-{vProvider.Id}")">
                            <Columns>
                                @* A model id is one token. Its hyphens are soft-wrap points, so without
                                   nowrap the column shrinks below the id and `claude-` sits above
                                   `fable-5` at 390px. The table scrolls in its own box instead. *@
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PriceProviderModel" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRate => aRate.Model)" Header="Model"
                                                 CellClass="@ModelCell" HeaderClass="@ModelHeader">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRate">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRate.Model</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                @* Align, not text-right: it reaches the th, the header label's own flex
                                   box and every body cell together, which is what puts "Input" over the
                                   figures instead of at the left of the column. *@
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PriceProviderModel" TValue="decimal"
                                                 Property="@(aRate => aRate.InputPerMillion)" Header="Input"
                                                 Align="DataTableColumnAlign.End"
                                                 CellClass="@RateCell" HeaderClass="@RateHeader">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRate">@Usd(vRate.InputPerMillion)</CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PriceProviderModel" TValue="decimal"
                                                 Property="@(aRate => aRate.OutputPerMillion)" Header="Output"
                                                 Align="DataTableColumnAlign.End"
                                                 CellClass="@RateCell" HeaderClass="@RateHeader">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRate">@Usd(vRate.OutputPerMillion)</CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PriceProviderModel" TValue="decimal"
                                                 Property="@(aRate => aRate.CacheReadPerMillion)" Header="Cache read"
                                                 Align="DataTableColumnAlign.End"
                                                 CellClass="@RateCell" HeaderClass="@RateHeader">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRate">@Usd(vRate.CacheReadPerMillion)</CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PriceProviderModel" TValue="decimal"
                                                 Property="@(aRate => aRate.CacheWritePerMillion)" Header="Cache write"
                                                 Align="DataTableColumnAlign.End"
                                                 CellClass="@RateCell" HeaderClass="@RateHeader">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRate">@Usd(vRate.CacheWritePerMillion)</CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    }
                </CardContent>

                <CardFooter Class="@(vPage.HasPager ? "tflens-prices-foot" : "tflens-prices-foot tflens-prices-foot-start")">
                    <span class="tflens-prices-hint">@FooterNote(vProvider, vPage)</span>
                    @if (vPage.HasPager)
                    {
                        <span class="inline-flex gap-2">
                            <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline"
                                    Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                    Disabled="@(!vPage.CanGoBack)"
                                    data-testid="@($"prices-page-prev-{vProvider.Id}")"
                                    OnClick="() => GoToPage(vProvider, vPage.PageIndex - 1)">
                                Previous
                            </Button>
                            <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline"
                                    Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                    Disabled="@(!vPage.CanGoForward)"
                                    data-testid="@($"prices-page-next-{vProvider.Id}")"
                                    OnClick="() => GoToPage(vProvider, vPage.PageIndex + 1)">
                                Next
                            </Button>
                        </span>
                    }
                </CardFooter>
            }
        </Card>
    }

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <Card data-testid="prices-add-provider">
            <CardHeader>
                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Add a provider</CardTitle>
                <CardDescription>
                    Give it the page a person can check the rates against. An endpoint is optional — only a
                    provider that publishes its rates as data can be refreshed, and today that is OpenRouter.
                </CardDescription>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-new-name">Name</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-new-name" @bind-Value="objNewName" Placeholder="e.g. Google"
                                   data-testid="prices-new-name" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-new-source">Published pricing page</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-new-source" Type="InputType.Url" @bind-Value="objNewSource"
                                   Placeholder="https://…" Class="font-mono" data-testid="prices-new-source" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-new-api">Endpoint (optional)</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-new-api" Type="InputType.Url" @bind-Value="objNewApi"
                                   Placeholder="https://…/models" Class="font-mono" data-testid="prices-new-api" />
                            <FieldDescription>Leave empty for a provider whose rates are typed from its page.</FieldDescription>
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter Class="tflens-prices-foot tflens-prices-foot-end">
                <Button Disabled="@objIsBusy" data-testid="prices-add" OnClick="AddAsync">
                    <LucideIcon Name="plus" Size="16" />
                    Add provider
                </Button>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        <Card data-testid="prices-add-rate">
            <CardHeader>
                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Add or change a rate</CardTitle>
                <CardDescription>
                    The model id must match what a run record names, exactly — that is what the rate is
                    matched on. A rate that matches nothing prices nothing and is never an error.
                </CardDescription>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-provider">Provider</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            @* NativeSelect, the library's own select over a real <select>: the list is
                               a handful of provider names, and a native control keeps the choice
                               keyboard- and test-drivable exactly as the mockup draws it. *@
                            <NativeSelect @bind-Value="objRateProvider"
                                          id="prices-rate-provider"
                                          data-testid="prices-rate-provider">
                                @foreach (var vProvider in objProviders)
                                {
                                    <option value="@vProvider.Id">@vProvider.Name</option>
                                }
                            </NativeSelect>
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-model">Model id</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-rate-model" @bind-Value="objRateModel" Placeholder="claude-opus-5"
                                   Class="font-mono" data-testid="prices-rate-model" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-in">Input / 1M</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-rate-in" @bind-Value="objRateIn" inputmode="decimal" data-testid="prices-rate-in" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-out">Output / 1M</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-rate-out" @bind-Value="objRateOut" inputmode="decimal" data-testid="prices-rate-out" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-cr">Cache read / 1M</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-rate-cr" @bind-Value="objRateCacheRead" inputmode="decimal" data-testid="prices-rate-cr" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                    <Field>
                        <FieldLabel For="prices-rate-cw">Cache write / 1M</FieldLabel>
                        <FieldContent>
                            <Input Id="prices-rate-cw" @bind-Value="objRateCacheWrite" inputmode="decimal" data-testid="prices-rate-cw" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                </div>
                <FieldDescription Class="mt-4">
                    USD per 1,000,000 tokens. A negative or non-numeric rate is refused and nothing is saved.
                </FieldDescription>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter Class="tflens-prices-foot tflens-prices-foot-end">
                <Button Disabled="@objIsBusy" data-testid="prices-save-rate" OnClick="SaveRateAsync">Save rate</Button>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>
    </div>

    @* The outcome of the last action sits under the forms, where the mockup draws it, and is brought
       into view when it changes. It is always in the page and hidden until there is something to say,
       so a Refresh pressed at the top of the page still lands the reader on its answer. *@
    <div class="tflens-prices-message" tabindex="-1" @ref="objMessageRef">
        <Alert Variant="@(objIsMessageProblem ? AlertVariant.Warning : AlertVariant.Info)"
               Class="@(objMessage is { Length: > 0 } ? null : "tflens-prices-message-idle")"
               data-testid="prices-message">
            <LucideIcon Name="@(objIsMessageProblem ? "triangle-alert" : "info")" Size="16" />
            <AlertDescription>@objMessage</AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // The mockup's rate table: a 10px/16px header cell and a 12px/16px body cell, over the grid's
    // own Compact density. A column's classes are merged after the density's, so these win; nothing
    // has to reach into the table from the page's stylesheet (TR-025).
    private const string CellPad = "px-4 py-3";
    private const string HeaderPad = "px-4 text-xs";

    private const string ModelCell = CellPad + " whitespace-nowrap";
    private const string ModelHeader = HeaderPad + " whitespace-nowrap";
    private const string RateCell = CellPad + " tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap";
    private const string RateHeader = HeaderPad + " whitespace-nowrap";

    private List<PriceProvider> objProviders = [];
    private IReadOnlyList<string> objClashes = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<string, int> objPages = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    private readonly Dictionary<string, string> objFilters = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    private bool objIsLoading = true;
    private bool objIsBusy;

    private string? objMessage;
    private bool objIsMessageProblem;
    private bool objIsMessageNew;
    private ElementReference objMessageRef;

    private string objNewName = string.Empty;
    private string objNewSource = string.Empty;
    private string objNewApi = string.Empty;

    private string objRateProvider = string.Empty;
    private string objRateModel = string.Empty;
    private string objRateIn = "0";
    private string objRateOut = "0";
    private string objRateCacheRead = "0";
    private string objRateCacheWrite = "0";

    /// <summary>The header badge: every rate the book holds, over every provider.</summary>
    private string CountLabel
    {
        get
        {
            var vRates = objProviders.Sum(aProvider => aProvider.Models.Count);
            var vProviders = objProviders.Count;

            return string.Create(
                CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
                $"{vRates} {(vRates == 1 ? "rate" : "rates")} over {vProviders} {(vProviders == 1 ? "provider" : "providers")}");
        }
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await ReloadAsync();
        objIsLoading = false;
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool aFirstRender)
    {
        if (!objIsMessageNew)
        {
            return;
        }

        objIsMessageNew = false;
        await objMessageRef.FocusAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Reads the provider book and the clashes it carries.</summary>
    /// <returns>The running read.</returns>
    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        objProviders = [.. await PriceProviders.LoadAsync(objOptions.Value.PriceProvidersPath)];
        objClashes = PriceProviders.Clashes(objProviders);
        objRateProvider = objProviders.FirstOrDefault()?.Id ?? string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>Writes the book and rewrites the flat card every figure is priced from.</summary>
    /// <returns>The running write.</returns>
    private async Task PersistAsync()
    {
        await PriceProviders.SaveAsync(objOptions.Value.PriceProvidersPath, objProviders);
        await PriceProviders.ApplyAsync(objOptions.Value.PricesPath, objProviders);
        objClashes = PriceProviders.Clashes(objProviders);
    }

    /// <summary>Shows the outcome of an action and brings it into view.</summary>
    /// <param name="aText">What happened.</param>
    /// <param name="aIsProblem">Whether it is something the reader has to act on.</param>
    private void Say(string aText, bool aIsProblem = false)
    {
        objMessage = aText;
        objIsMessageProblem = aIsProblem;
        objIsMessageNew = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reads a provider's rates from its own endpoint.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// A failure leaves the stored rates exactly as they were and says so. Replacing a checked rate
    /// with nothing because a request timed out would turn a priced estate into an unpriced one with
    /// no record of why. A rate the endpoint declines to publish (OpenRouter's <c>-1</c>) is skipped by
    /// <see cref="PriceProviders.ReadOpenRouter"/>, never stored and never coerced to zero.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider to refresh.</param>
    /// <returns>The running refresh.</returns>
    private async Task RefreshAsync(PriceProvider aProvider)
    {
        objIsBusy = true;

        try
        {
            var vModels = await FetchAsync(aProvider);

            if (vModels.Count == 0)
            {
                Say($"{aProvider.Name} returned no rates this reader could understand. The stored rates are unchanged.", true);
                return;
            }

            Replace(aProvider, aProvider with { Models = vModels, LastChecked = Today() });
            objPages.Remove(aProvider.Id);
            await PersistAsync();
            Say($"{aProvider.Name}: {vModels.Count} rate(s) read from its endpoint.");
        }
        catch (Exception vError) when (vError is HttpRequestException or TaskCanceledException or JsonException)
        {
            Say($"{aProvider.Name} could not be reached ({vError.GetType().Name}). The stored rates are unchanged.", true);
        }
        catch (ArgumentOutOfRangeException vError)
        {
            // A rate the endpoint published that this page will not store. It is reported rather than
            // swallowed: the operator should know the provider sent something unusable.
            Say($"{aProvider.Name} published a rate that cannot be stored ({vError.ActualValue}). The stored rates are unchanged.", true);
        }
        finally
        {
            objIsBusy = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Calls a provider's endpoint and reads the rates out of its answer.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <returns>The rates it published; empty when none could be read.</returns>
    private async Task<IReadOnlyList<PriceProviderModel>> FetchAsync(PriceProvider aProvider)
    {
        using var vClient = objHttpClientFactory.CreateClient();
        vClient.Timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30);

        var vJson = await vClient.GetStringAsync(aProvider.ApiUrl!);

        return PriceProviders.ReadOpenRouter(vJson);
    }

    /// <summary>Adds a provider with no rates yet.</summary>
    /// <returns>The running add.</returns>
    private async Task AddAsync()
    {
        var vName = objNewName.Trim();
        var vId = IdOf(vName);

        if (vId.Length == 0)
        {
            Say("A provider needs a name.", true);
            return;
        }

        if (objProviders.Any(aProvider => string.Equals(aProvider.Id, vId, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))
        {
            Say($"A provider called {vName} is already listed.", true);
            return;
        }

        objIsBusy = true;

        try
        {
            objProviders.Add(NewProvider(vId, vName));
            await PersistAsync();
            Say($"{vName} added. It prices nothing until it has a rate.");
            objNewName = objNewSource = objNewApi = string.Empty;
        }
        finally
        {
            objIsBusy = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Builds the provider the Add form describes.</summary>
    /// <param name="aId">Its key.</param>
    /// <param name="aName">Its name.</param>
    /// <returns>The provider, with no rates and never checked.</returns>
    private PriceProvider NewProvider(string aId, string aName)
    {
        var vApi = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(objNewApi) ? null : objNewApi.Trim();

        return new PriceProvider(
            aId,
            aName,
            string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(objNewSource) ? null : objNewSource.Trim(),
            vApi,
            vApi is null ? PriceFetch.Manual : PriceFetch.Api,
            null,
            []);
    }

    /// <summary>Removes a provider and re-applies the flat card without its rates.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider to remove.</param>
    /// <returns>The running removal.</returns>
    private async Task RemoveAsync(PriceProvider aProvider)
    {
        objIsBusy = true;

        try
        {
            objProviders.Remove(aProvider);
            objPages.Remove(aProvider.Id);
            objFilters.Remove(aProvider.Id);

            if (string.Equals(objRateProvider, aProvider.Id, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            {
                objRateProvider = objProviders.FirstOrDefault()?.Id ?? string.Empty;
            }

            await PersistAsync();
            Say($"{aProvider.Name} removed. Any model only it priced now reports as unpriced.");
        }
        finally
        {
            objIsBusy = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Adds or replaces one model's rate on a provider.</summary>
    /// <returns>The running save.</returns>
    private async Task SaveRateAsync()
    {
        var vProvider = objProviders.FirstOrDefault(aProvider => aProvider.Id == objRateProvider);
        var vModel = objRateModel.Trim();

        if (vProvider is null || vModel.Length == 0)
        {
            Say("Choose a provider and give the model id a run record would carry.", true);
            return;
        }

        if (TypedRate(vModel) is not { } vRate)
        {
            Say("Every rate must be a number and none of them may be negative. Nothing was saved.", true);
            return;
        }

        objIsBusy = true;

        try
        {
            var vUpdated = WithRate(vProvider, vRate);
            Replace(vProvider, vUpdated);
            await PersistAsync();
            ShowModel(vUpdated, vModel);
            Say($"{vModel} priced on {vProvider.Name}.");
            objRateModel = string.Empty;
        }
        finally
        {
            objIsBusy = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Reads the four typed rates into one model's rate line.</summary>
    /// <param name="aModel">The model id.</param>
    /// <returns>The rate line, or <c>null</c> when any rate is not a usable number.</returns>
    private PriceProviderModel? TypedRate(string aModel) =>
        TryRate(objRateIn, out var vIn) && TryRate(objRateOut, out var vOut)
            && TryRate(objRateCacheRead, out var vCacheRead) && TryRate(objRateCacheWrite, out var vCacheWrite)
            ? new PriceProviderModel(aModel, vIn, vOut, vCacheRead, vCacheWrite)
            : null;

    /// <summary>A provider with one model's rate added, or replaced when it already had one.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <param name="aRate">The rate line.</param>
    /// <returns>The provider as it now stands, checked today.</returns>
    private static PriceProvider WithRate(PriceProvider aProvider, PriceProviderModel aRate) =>
        aProvider with
        {
            Models = aProvider.Models
                .Where(aModel => !string.Equals(aModel.Model, aRate.Model, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                .Append(aRate)
                .ToList(),
            LastChecked = Today()
        };

    /// <summary>Puts a changed provider back in its place in the list.</summary>
    /// <param name="aBefore">The provider as it was.</param>
    /// <param name="aAfter">The provider as it now is.</param>
    private void Replace(PriceProvider aBefore, PriceProvider aAfter) =>
        objProviders[objProviders.IndexOf(aBefore)] = aAfter;

    /// <summary>Turns a provider's pager to the page a model sits on, clearing its filter.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <param name="aModel">The model id.</param>
    private void ShowModel(PriceProvider aProvider, string aModel)
    {
        objFilters.Remove(aProvider.Id);
        objPages[aProvider.Id] = PriceRatePage.PageOf(aProvider.Models, aModel);
    }

    /// <summary>The page of a provider's rates the reader is on.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <returns>The page.</returns>
    private PriceRatePage PageFor(PriceProvider aProvider) =>
        PriceRatePage.Of(aProvider.Models, FilterOf(aProvider), objPages.GetValueOrDefault(aProvider.Id));

    /// <summary>The filter typed over a provider's rates.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <returns>The filter text; empty when none.</returns>
    private string FilterOf(PriceProvider aProvider) => objFilters.GetValueOrDefault(aProvider.Id) ?? string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Narrows a provider's rates to the model ids containing the typed text.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <param name="aText">The text typed.</param>
    private void OnFilterChanged(PriceProvider aProvider, string? aText)
    {
        objFilters[aProvider.Id] = aText ?? string.Empty;
        objPages[aProvider.Id] = 0;
    }

    /// <summary>Moves a provider's pager.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <param name="aPageIndex">The zero-based page wanted.</param>
    private void GoToPage(PriceProvider aProvider, int aPageIndex) => objPages[aProvider.Id] = Math.Max(0, aPageIndex);

    /// <summary>The footer line: the unit, the page count, and for an endpoint what it never stores.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <param name="aPage">The page shown.</param>
    /// <returns>The line.</returns>
    private static string FooterNote(PriceProvider aProvider, PriceRatePage aPage)
    {
        var vParts = new List<string> { "USD per 1,000,000 tokens" };

        if (aPage.Summary is { } vSummary)
        {
            vParts.Add(vSummary);
        }

        if (IsEndpoint(aProvider))
        {
            vParts.Add("a rate the endpoint declines to publish is skipped, never stored as zero");
        }

        return string.Join(" · ", vParts);
    }

    /// <summary>Whether a provider's rates are read from its own endpoint rather than typed.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <returns><c>true</c> for an endpoint provider.</returns>
    private static bool IsEndpoint(PriceProvider aProvider) => aProvider.Fetch == PriceFetch.Api;

    /// <summary>The last-checked badge text.</summary>
    /// <param name="aProvider">The provider.</param>
    /// <returns>"last checked" and the date, or "never checked".</returns>
    private static string CheckedLabel(PriceProvider aProvider) =>
        aProvider.LastChecked is { Length: > 0 } vChecked ? $"last checked {vChecked}" : "never checked";

    /// <summary>A provider's key, from its name: lower case, anything but a letter or digit a hyphen.</summary>
    /// <param name="aName">The name.</param>
    /// <returns>The key; empty for a blank name.</returns>
    private static string IdOf(string aName) =>
        new(aName.ToLowerInvariant().Select(aChar => char.IsLetterOrDigit(aChar) ? aChar : '-').ToArray());

    /// <summary>Today's date as the book stores it.</summary>
    /// <returns>The date, <c>yyyy-MM-dd</c>, UTC.</returns>
    private static string Today() => DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    /// <summary>Reads one typed rate, refusing a negative one.</summary>
    /// <param name="aText">What the operator typed.</param>
    /// <param name="aRate">The parsed rate.</param>
    /// <returns><c>true</c> when it is a usable rate.</returns>
    private static bool TryRate(string aText, out decimal aRate) =>
        decimal.TryParse(aText, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out aRate) && aRate >= 0m;

    /// <summary>Renders one rate.</summary>
    /// <param name="aRate">The rate.</param>
    /// <returns>The display string.</returns>
    private static string Usd(decimal aRate) => "$" + aRate.ToString("0.####", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
}
